@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ArrowColor #3F5E52
skinparam BorderColor #AFC2B9
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F7FAF8
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F2F7F4
skinparam NodeBackgroundColor #FBFCFB

title Wago runtime architecture
left to right direction

actor "Operator\nBrowser" as Operator
actor "External\nAPI client" as ApiClient
cloud "WhatsApp Web" as WhatsApp

node "Wago container" as Container {
  rectangle "React dashboard\nControl · Settings · Audit Log" as Frontend

  package "Express 5 application" as Backend {
    rectangle "HTTP transport\nmiddleware · auth attachment\nrequest / response mapping" as Http
    rectangle "Capability modules\naccess · activity · gateway · messages\nmetrics · recipients · webhooks · whatsapp" as Modules
    rectangle "Application composition\nand lifecycle" as App
    rectangle "Infrastructure\nSQLite · migrations · logging\nmount / lease safety" as Infrastructure
  }

  database "SQLite durable state\n/app/data/wago.db" as Database
  database "Baileys auth files\n/app/data/auth/" as AuthFiles
  collections "Transient runtime state\nQR · connection/reconnect\naccount-health cache" as Memory
}

Operator --> Frontend : HTTPS
Frontend --> Http : same-origin API
ApiClient --> Http : HTTPS + Bearer
Http --> Modules
App --> Modules : compose / coordinate
Modules --> Infrastructure
Infrastructure --> Database
Modules --> AuthFiles : WhatsApp credential lifecycle
Modules --> Memory : ephemeral runtime state
Modules <--> WhatsApp : Baileys / WhatsApp Web

note bottom of Database
SQLite is the authoritative application store.
Settings, browser sessions, binding, recipients,
outbound diagnostics/policy, webhook state,
and audit evidence are durable here.
end note

note bottom of Modules
Baileys protocol details stay inside the WhatsApp owner.
Audit and diagnostics keep sanitized metadata only;
secret-bearing and message-body data is not retained unnecessarily.
end note

note bottom of Container
One process, one persistent /app/data volume,
and one WhatsApp account per deployed instance.
end note
@enduml
